exists su name chirp source thrust intent ob text quoted.text.The generator is asked to compress the source into a short evergreen social post or one short supporting atom candidate. It may heighten clarity, compression, and slight surprise, but it must not add unsupported concrete claims, actors, dates, statistics, policies, or mechanisms beyond the source..text.quoted be text ya

exists su name chirp problem prompt ob text quoted.text.You are writing candidate problem atoms for a short evergreen social post.

Task:
- Write up to 5 candidate lines.
- Each line must be one short sentence naming the visible pain, confusion, or wrong frame.
- Keep each line between 6 and 16 words.
- Keep each line between 30 and 95 characters.

Rules:
- Ground every line in the source text.
- Do not assume what "people think" or "everyone believes".
- Do not add unsupported concrete claims.
- Make each line crisp and plain.
- End each line with ".".
- Output one candidate per line.
- No numbering, no bullets, no markdown, no surrounding quotes..text.quoted be text ya

exists su name chirp cause prompt ob text quoted.text.You are writing candidate hidden-cause atoms for a short evergreen social post.

Task:
- Write up to 5 candidate lines.
- Each line must be one short sentence naming the hidden driver, constraint, incentive, or tradeoff.
- Keep each line between 6 and 18 words.
- Keep each line between 35 and 110 characters.

Rules:
- Ground every line in the source text.
- Do not add unsupported concrete claims or mechanisms.
- Prefer a clear causal or structural frame over rhetoric.
- End each line with ".".
- Output one candidate per line.
- No numbering, no bullets, no markdown, no surrounding quotes..text.quoted be text ya

exists su name chirp insight prompt ob text quoted.text.You are writing candidate insight atoms for a short evergreen social post.

Task:
- Write up to 5 candidate lines.
- Each line must be one short sentence giving the upgraded frame, rule, or lever.
- Keep each line between 6 and 18 words.
- Keep each line between 30 and 110 characters.

Rules:
- Ground every line in the source text.
- Do not add unsupported concrete claims.
- Make each line memorable but not grandiose.
- Avoid identity labels or ideological framing unless the source clearly requires them.
- End each line with ".".
- Output one candidate per line.
- No numbering, no bullets, no markdown, no surrounding quotes..text.quoted be text ya

exists su name chirp proof prompt ob text quoted.text.You are writing candidate proof-hook atoms for a short evergreen social post.

Task:
- Write up to 4 candidate lines.
- Each line must be one short sentence containing a small supporting element from the source.
- This can be a micro-example, vivid phrase, or tiny concrete support.
- Keep each line between 4 and 16 words.
- Keep each line between 20 and 90 characters.

Rules:
- Ground every line in the source text.
- Do not add unsupported concrete claims.
- Keep each line compact.
- End each line with ".".
- Output one candidate per line.
- No numbering, no bullets, no markdown, no surrounding quotes..text.quoted be text ya

exists su name chirp boundary prompt ob text quoted.text.You are writing candidate boundary atoms for a short evergreen social post.

Task:
- Write up to 4 candidate lines.
- Each line must be one short sentence naming a caveat, limit, or scope boundary that keeps the claim honest.
- Keep each line between 4 and 16 words.
- Keep each line between 20 and 90 characters.

Rules:
- Ground every line in the source text.
- Do not add unsupported concrete claims.
- Keep each line plain and useful.
- Avoid identity labels or ideological framing unless the source clearly requires them.
- End each line with ".".
- Output one candidate per line.
- No numbering, no bullets, no markdown, no surrounding quotes..text.quoted be text ya

exists su name chirp template prompt ob text quoted.text.You are choosing the best evergreen template family for a short chirp manuscript.

Choose exactly one of these outputs:
- definition pivot
- symptom to root cause
- incentive lens
- hidden cost reveal
- diagnostic test

Use the source and candidate pools below.
Candidate pools contain one candidate per line and may contain blank lines from rejected candidates. Ignore blank lines.
Pick the family that fits the strongest surviving candidates while making the fewest unsupported assumptions.
Prefer the cleanest mechanism over the flashiest framing.

Return exactly one template family from the allowed list.
No explanation.
No punctuation.
No extra words..text.quoted be text ya

exists su name chirp problem sieve prompt ob text quoted.text.You are filtering candidate problem atoms for a short evergreen social post.

You will receive:
- SOURCE
- CANDIDATES with one candidate per line

Keep only lines that pass all checks:
- grounded in the source
- 6 to 16 words
- 30 to 95 characters
- one complete short sentence
- no numbering, bullets, or markdown
- no vague "people think" or "everyone believes" assumptions
- no unsupported concrete claims

Output rules:
- Return only the passing lines, exactly as written, one per line.
- Preserve original wording for kept lines.
- Drop failing lines entirely.
- You may return fewer than 5 lines, or none.
- No explanations, no labels, no extra text..text.quoted be text ya

